closed form equals enumeration on 12 of 12 items
Part 2 · Monty Hall, exact enumeration of (car, pick, host door)
host always opens a goat door: P(stay wins) = 1/3, P(switch wins) = 2/3
host opens at random, given a goat: P(stay wins) = 1/2, P(switch wins) = 1/2
the two host rules give different answers: True
Part 3 · Bayes' rule on two bags, exact enumeration of (bag, ball)
P(red) = 1/2
P(bag 1 | red) by enumeration = 3/4
P(bag 1 | red) by Bayes' rule = 3/4
Part 4 · two fair coins and an urn, exact enumeration
P(both heads | at least one head) = 1/3
P(both heads | first flip heads) = 1/2
P(at least one head | both heads) = 1
P(both heads) = 1/4
P(second red) = 3/5
P(first red) = 3/5
P(first red and second red) = 3/10
P(second red) equals P(first red): True
P(second red | first blue) = 3/4
